name: analyze-swarag
description: Run multi-agent analysis on a Swarag issue

---

Analyze this issue using the Swarag 5-agent engineering team.

Before answering, read the project memory files:
- .ai-memory/bugs.md
- .ai-memory/lessons.md
- .ai-memory/architecture.md
- .ai-memory/datasets.md
- .ai-memory/debug-playbook.md

Then simulate these 5 experts, each analyzing the problem from their domain:

1. AUDIO DSP ENGINEER
   Focus: pitch extraction, tonic drift, gamaka, audio quality

2. MIR RESEARCHER
   Focus: raga grammar, feature discriminative power, musical validity

3. MACHINE LEARNING ENGINEER
   Focus: scoring calibration, similarity metrics, penalty logic, margins

4. SOFTWARE ARCHITECT
   Focus: interface contracts, dependencies, constant sync, architectural drift

5. DEBUG INVESTIGATOR
   Focus: file paths, data loading, empty arrays, shapes, silent errors

Format your response as:

[Audio DSP]   -> finding
[MIR]         -> finding
[ML Engineer] -> finding
[Architect]   -> finding
[Debug]       -> finding

AGREEMENTS (high-confidence findings where multiple experts agree):
- ...

DISAGREEMENTS (areas needing deeper investigation):
- ...

UNIFIED RECOMMENDATION:
Priority-ordered action plan based on the combined analysis.
